A repite contratos en otros años. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se agrupan en un mismo área.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 86 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 15.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.2 to 7.9. December accounts for 6% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 4% of all its services and supplies contracts. Contract [1], for 14,999.23 euros, was awarded in December 2025. Contract [3], for 14,900 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or multiple separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts to see if they align with the body's needs. Review the awardee A contracts to see if they repeat the same services or products. Look at the December contracts to determine if they were part of a larger pattern or isolated events.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["X5k%2FWkbA6jA7u6%2B%2FR7DUoA%3D%3D","rqoHpSKhoEkeIBJRHQiPkQ%3D%3D","fBYrfXLzKgGKeVWTb9Scog%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}